 0.0}, "rating_margin": null, "sigma_race": 9.0, "sigma_total": 11.26, "baseline_margin": 0.0, "analyst_adjustment": 0.0, "key_factors": ["Even partisan lean leaves Wisconsin with no net advantage for either party", "No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices yet available", "Term-limited president removes incumbency effects from an open race", "2026 headlines show a volatile, closely divided electorate"], "rationale": "Wisconsin's dead-even partisan lean and history of razor-thin results make it the definition of a battleground, and with no polls, ratings, or prices yet published, fundamentals alone point to a coin-flip race.", "watch": "The first credible general-election polls and the parties' eventual nominees could quickly tip the balance either way.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin enters the 2028 presidential race as the purest tossup on the map. The state carries no partisan lean, its recent presidential contests have been decided by the narrowest margins in the country, and the term-limited presidency removes any incumbency advantage for either side. With no general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices yet published, the forecast rests entirely on fundamentals, and those fundamentals are dead even.\n\nThe 2026 campaign offered hints of the state's volatility: the governor's race stayed tight into the fall, and disputes over election certification kept Wisconsin's pivotal role in future results in the headlines. None of that yet translates into a measurable edge for either party's presidential ticket. Until credible polling or ratings arrive, an even split of the vote with a wide range of possible outcomes is the most defensible read.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem"